  "note": "hidden_from_faction_ids is real NodeDef schema (Decision 28, specs/15): factions that do not know the node exists at map start. links are the authored, intended routes (Decision 26): only linked pairs connect. Each link's route is its initial geometry, pathfound across terrain cost (cheaper on roads, impassable water without a bridge, other nodes not enterable); unlinked pairs never get a route. WAYPOINT is a real NodeType (specs/16); nodes on no lane are imported as MapDef.off_lane_nodes; structure_slots no longer exists (Decision 25). PROTOTYPE-ONLY (no Godot schema yet, design notes on file): is_critical_asset, loss_criteria (groups OR'd; each group ANY/ALL of its nodes), the tiles layer stack (terrain, feature, bridge, stability/max_height/max_width capacity, upgrades), roads (explicit 8-neighbour cell pairs; movement modifier, not topology), node structure (Decision 27, Godot-shaped for a future StructureDef: a 2D side-on plane; approaches say which end (LEFT/RIGHT) each linked route enters; segments -> SegmentDef {col, level (negative = basement), label, features, emplacements}; boundaries -> BoundaryDef {kind WALL/FLOOR/ROOF_ACCESS, col, level, exterior_side, outside, preset, blocks_movement_from, blocks_projectiles_from, blocks_sight_from (sides LEFT/RIGHT/ABOVE/BELOW), fortification, material}; roofs -> RoofDef {col, type, emplacements}; ranged_positions = firing positions any ranged unit can use; manning = emplacement crews from the garrison; archetype is art only; stability = total segment budget), terrain_library/feature_library/road_move_multiplier (stubs). tiles lists only cells with at least one explicit layer; any other cell is plain default_terrain. garrison_count is derived from garrison_units.length. _display_label is prototype-only. factions is this map's roster only; library default relations are not exported."
}
